* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-vco-period-jitter (issue #518, Part of #16)
* Calibration stage transient-noise validation: the same DC-stable stage
* as tb_cal_noise.sp.tmpl with the calibrated aggregate white noise current
* actually injected (the same trrandom source form, sample interval and
* sigma the ring decks use).  The transient output-noise PSD, computed from
* this run's waveform, must reproduce the .noise output spectral density
* over the jitter band within the tolerance RECORD-001 states -- this is
* the end-to-end check of the injection mechanism (source form, ZOH
* spectrum, solver behaviour), not just of the analytic fit.
*
* The waveform is written by wrdata to calpsd.txt (2 us at a uniform 5 ps
* grid after `linearize`); ../testbench/extract.py Welch-averages it.
*
* Template placeholders: @SIGMA@ (A, rms), @TS@ (noise sample interval, s),
* @SEED@ (setseed value), plus the shared set (see tb_bias_op.sp.tmpl).
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!
.include vco_open.spice
vbiasp vbp 0 dc @VBP@
vbiasn vbn 0 dc @VBN@
vdd vdd 0 dc 3.3
vsub sub! 0 dc 0
xs1 sin1 vbp vbn sout vdd 0 vco_stage
rfb sout sin1 1e12
inj sout 0 dc 0 trrandom(2, @TS@, 0, @SIGMA@)
.tran @TSTEP@ 2u
.control
pre_osdi @OSDI@/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi @OSDI@/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi @OSDI@/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi @OSDI@/r3_cmc.osdi
setseed @SEED@
run
linearize v(sout)
wrdata calpsd.txt v(sout)
.endc
.end
